+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Orders can be created and coupons can be administered, but the two never meet: there
+is no way to redeem a coupon against an order, so `orders.discount_cents` and
+`orders.coupon_code` stay empty and `coupon_redemptions` is never written. Customers
+cannot actually receive the discounts the coupon catalog advertises.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "<code>" }`.
+- Validate the coupon before discounting: it must exist, be `ACTIVE`, be inside its
+  `validFrom`/`validUntil` window, satisfy the order amount against
+  `minAmountCents`, and not have exhausted its `usageLimit`.
+- Compute the discount from the order's original amount: `FIXED` subtracts the
+  coupon value, `PERCENT` applies the percentage, both honoring an optional
+  `maxDiscountCents` cap and never exceeding the order amount.
+- Persist `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents` and `coupon_code` on the order and
+  record the redemption in `coupon_redemptions`, incrementing `used_count`.
+- Return the updated order with HTTP 200 for an applicable coupon; return HTTP 400
+  for any coupon that cannot be applied (missing, disabled, expired/not yet valid,
+  below minimum, exhausted).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `coupon-redemption`: deciding whether a coupon may be applied to an order and how
+  the resulting discount and final amount are computed and recorded.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- No existing capabilities in `openspec/specs/`; nothing is being modified. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts` — register the new route.
+- `src/services/orderService.ts` — discount rules and validation of the coupon.
+- `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` — persist discount, final amount and coupon.
+- `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts` — redemption recording and `used_count`.
+- `src/app.ts` — give the order service access to coupons.
+- No schema, dependency or API-breaking changes.
